\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces Corpus composition. Each category is drawn from exactly one source dataset, which is the confound discussed throughout: category and provenance cannot be separated.}}{22}{table.caption.16}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Signed index by category over all 400 scanned items. Every category mean is negative, so deliberative activation leads throughout.}}{27}{table.caption.17}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces Classifier performance against the pre-scan manipulative label. AUC is the headline figure; the threshold behind F1 was fitted in sample and F1 is labelled accordingly.}}{28}{table.caption.18}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces Baselines against the same manipulative label. The lower block restricts the corpus to the 150 items drawn from the ISOT collection, the only origin corpus contributing both classes.}}{29}{table.caption.19}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.4}{\ignorespaces Welch comparisons of each category against neutral informational. The separation is carried by fear-activating content; high outrage does not separate, and it is the category the proposal expected to separate most.}}{31}{table.caption.20}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.5}{\ignorespaces Category means of each component and of their difference, over all 400 items.}}{32}{table.caption.23}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.6}{\ignorespaces Welch comparisons of each component against neutral informational. High outrage moves both components by nearly the same amount and the difference between them by nothing; fear-activating content moves one component only.}}{33}{table.caption.24}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.7}{\ignorespaces The field bound at three values of the reduced coupling. The measured spread $\Delta X = 0.1241$ converts each critical field into the coupling any proposal of this mechanism would require.}}{36}{table.caption.28}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.8}{\ignorespaces Smallest effects this design could detect at $\alpha = 0.05$ and power $0.80$, fixed before the corpus was analysed.}}{37}{table.caption.29}%
